// Test: bugfixes/list_namespace_functions_check_element_type
// Grammar: method_call
// Semantic: SEM001 — the values given to `items.add(...)`, `.set`, `.insert`
//   and `.contains` must have the list's element type
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.183
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   list_namespace_functions_check_element_type.cln:24
//   list_namespace_functions_check_element_type.cln:25
//   list_namespace_functions_check_element_type.cln:26
//   list_namespace_functions_check_element_type.cln:23
//   A value of type string cannot be used as integer
//
// Regression: `list.add(numbers, "zz")` stored a string pointer in a list of
// integers (`l[2]` printed an address).
//
// Changed in 0.33.184: `list.<method>(items, ...)` namespace calls are now the
// method form `items.<method>(...)`; the `list.` namespace has only concat,
// range, fill and join (developer decision)

start:
	list<integer> l = [1, 2]
	l.add("zz")
	l.set(0, "zz")
	l.insert(0, "zz")
	boolean b = l.contains("zz")
	print(b.toString())
